{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureRef"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:10GLibObject10ClosureRefV","title":"ClosureRef","modules":[{"name":"GLibObject"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClosureRef","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClosureRef","kind":"identifier"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClosureRef"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It will generally comprise a function of some kind and a marshaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used to call it. It is the responsibility of the marshaller to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"convert the arguments for the invocation from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"#struct@Value"},{"type":"text","text":" into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a suitable form, perform the callback on the converted arguments,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and transform the return value back into a [struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Value","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the case of C programs, a closure usually just holds a pointer"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to a function and maybe a data argument, and the marshaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converts between [struct"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Value","isActive":true},{"text":"] and native C types. The GObject","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"library provides the [struct"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/CClosure","type":"reference"},{"text":"] type for this purpose. Bindings for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other languages need marshallers which convert between "},{"identifier":"#struct@Value","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"GValues","type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"GValues","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and suitable representations in the runtime of the language in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order to use functions written in that language as callbacks. Use","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"code":"Closure.set_marshal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] to set the marshaller on such a custom"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"closure implementation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Within GObject, closures play an important role in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"implementation of signals. When a signal is registered, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"c_marshaller"},{"type":"text","text":" argument to [func"},{"code":"signal_new","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] specifies the default C","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"marshaller for any closure which is connected to this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signal. GObject provides a number of C marshallers for this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"purpose, see the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_cclosure_marshal_*()"},{"type":"text","text":" functions. Additional C"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"marshallers can be generated with the "},{"identifier":"#glib-genmarshal","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"utility.  Closures can be explicitly connected to signals with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"code":"signal_connect_closure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], but it usually more convenient to let"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"GObject create a closure automatically by using one of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_signal_connect_*()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" functions which take a callback function\/user","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"data pair.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Using closures has a number of important advantages over a simple","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback function\/data pointer combination:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Closures allow the callee to get the types of the callback parameters,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which means that language bindings don’t have to write individual glue"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for each callback type.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The reference counting of [struct"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Closure"},{"text":"] makes it easy to handle reentrancy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right; if a callback is removed while it is being invoked, the closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and its parameters won’t be freed until the invocation finishes.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Closure.invalidate"},{"type":"text","text":"] and invalidation notifiers allow callbacks to be"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically removed when the objects they point to go away.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureRef","type":"reference"},{"text":" type acts as a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GClosure"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It exposes methods that can operate on this data type through ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureProtocol","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureRef","isActive":true},{"text":" only as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference to an existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GClosure"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Closure","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") if you want to use Automatic Reference Counting for memory management of the underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GClosure"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GClosure"},{"text":" represents a callback supplied by the programmer.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"